       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Adelaide Strikers sign Haris Rauf for full BBL|16 season</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Adelaide Strikers have signed Pakistan pace bowler Haris Rauf for the entire KFC BBL|16 season. The 32-year-old, who previously played 33 matches for the Melbourne Stars, joins international recruits Ben Stokes and Mark Chapman to bolster the Strikers' squad under head coach Tim Paine.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/adelaide-strikers-sign-haris-rauf-for-full-bbl16-season.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rauf is Pakistan's second-highest T20 international wicket-taker and was a joint winner of the Golden Arm award in BBL|15. The Strikers, led by captain Matt Short, have now filled all three overseas player slots as they look to improve their performance in the upcoming tournament.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the transfer details, international recruits, and historical context provided in the source.</p>
