     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · BBC Health · 2026-11-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Belfast City Hospital Introduces Robotic Surgery for Endometriosis</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#health</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Belfast City Hospital has introduced a Da Vinci surgical robot, the first of its kind on the island of Ireland, to treat complex gynaecological conditions. Funded by £2.4 million in charitable donations, the system has completed 130 surgeries since May, primarily for patients with chronic endometriosis. Four consultants have been trained to operate the technology, which offers increased precision in tight pelvic spaces.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/belfast-city-hospital-introduces-robotic-surgery-for-endomet.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This development aims to address significant waiting lists that have historically forced many women to endure years of chronic pain. Colleen Crothers, who experienced years of delays before undergoing conventional surgery, expressed hope that the robot will prevent future patients from suffering similar long-term complications.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise summary of the robot's implementation and impact. It captures both the technical utility and the human context of the waiting lists effectively.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c98rz8v5rem0o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Health</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
