       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · BBC Business · 2026-11-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Charities Report Rising Demand for Christmas Gift Appeals</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Charities across the UK report a surge in demand for Christmas gift donations as more families struggle with the cost of living crisis. The Chard Christmas Present Appeal and Taunton’s Christmas Sparkle have both seen a sharp increase in requests from schools, social services, and police. Despite higher need, organizations report a decline in donations as financial pressures impact potential donors.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/charities-report-rising-demand-for-christmas-gift-appeals.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Christmas Sparkle, which distributed 10,000 individual gifts last year, anticipates further growth in requests this season. Organizers highlight that many families are struggling to afford basic necessities, often requesting simple items like stationery. Charities are relying entirely on public donations to provide toys and support to vulnerable households.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects the surge in demand and the decline in donations mentioned in the source.</p>
