     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Independent Candidates May Decide Vizianagaram Municipal Polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Independent candidates are expected to serve as kingmakers in the Vizianagaram municipal elections following a 62.73% voter turnout. Analysts suggest their performance will be decisive in tight races between YSRCP and the NDA alliance, where margins are projected to be between 3,500 and 4,500 votes.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/independent-candidates-may-decide-vizianagaram-municipal-pol.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>With 169 candidates contesting for 62 divisions, the major parties are worried about cross-voting and the impact of independents. While counting for the mayoral and corporator posts is scheduled for Tuesday at designated venues, the outcome remains uncertain as candidates await results.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise summary that accurately reflects the source's data on turnout and the potential impact of independent candidates.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
