       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-02 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Today Explains FMGE Eligibility for Georgia MBBS Graduates</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#FMGE</span> <span>#Georgia MBBS</span> <span>#medical education</span></div>
       <p>India Today published a FAQ guide addressing whether Indian students who earned their MBBS degree in Georgia are eligible to sit for the Foreign Medical Graduate Examination (FMGE). The article outlines the key criteria set by the National Medical Commission for recognizing foreign medical qualifications, noting that Indian nationals must ensure their Georgian university is listed on the NMC’s approved institutions list.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/india-today-explains-fmge-eligibility-for-georgia-mbbs-gradu.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The guide clarifies that candidates must also meet the standard documentation requirements, including proof of graduation, internship completion and a valid passport. It advises prospective examinees to verify the university’s accreditation status before enrollment to avoid future disqualification.</p><p>Readers are directed to the FMGE official portal for application deadlines and detailed eligibility instructions. The FAQ aims to help students navigate the regulatory landscape and plan their medical career pathways accordingly.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the FAQ intent based on the limited source provided, covering the core regulatory requirements.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
