       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-02 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Indian B-Schools Witness 11% Drop in Domestic Demand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#b-schools</span> <span>#education</span> <span>#domestic demand</span> <span>#Europe</span></div>
       <p>Indian business schools (b-schools) have experienced an 11% drop in domestic demand, according to a report by The Financial Express. This decline indicates a shift in student preferences and educational trends within the country.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/indian-b-schools-witness-11-drop-in-domestic-demand.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The decrease in domestic demand for Indian b-schools coincides with a period where b-schools in Europe and Asia are reportedly gaining ground. This suggests that a portion of prospective students may now be opting for international educational opportunities in these regions over domestic programs.</p><p>What to watch: The continuing trends in student mobility for business education.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate, though thin due to the limited nature of the source summary provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
