     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Nagarkurnool administration issues safety protocols for Cyclone Murasu</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Nagarkurnool district administration has issued a list of safety guidelines as Cyclone Murasu intensifies into a severe storm over the Bay of Bengal. Residents are urged to avoid travel to Somasila and the Nallamalla ghat road, stay away from water bodies, and refrain from standing near trees or electric poles.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/nagarkurnool-administration-issues-safety-protocols-for-cycl.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Collector Hemanta Keshav Patil advised farmers to secure cattle and take precautions for agricultural assets. Heavy to very heavy rainfall is forecast for the district, prompting the establishment of a dedicated helpline at 08540-230201 to manage emergencies. The district expects strong gusty winds and lightning through Tuesday.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the administration's guidelines and the cyclone's impact.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/cyclone-murasu-telanganas-nagarkurnool-administration-releases-dos-and-donts/article71655531.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
