     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Namma Metro Pink Line Likely to Open November 13</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Bangalore South MP L.S. Tejasvi Surya indicated that the 7.5-km elevated Pink Line of Namma Metro is likely to be inaugurated on November 13. While the State government previously signaled a mid-November opening, BMRCL officials state they have not yet received formal confirmation from the Prime Minister’s Office.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/namma-metro-pink-line-likely-to-open-november-13.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The new stretch covers six stations, including Kalena Agrahara and Jayadeva Hospital, and will expand the operational network to 103.60 km. Once fully functional, the full 21.3-km line will connect the southern and central parts of Bengaluru, providing a vital link for commuters.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures the key details regarding the potential inauguration date and the current status of the Pink Line accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/bangalore/pink-line-likely-to-be-inaugurated-on-november-13/article71657962.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
