       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-11-02 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Russia Media Argues India Should Acquire Su‑57 to Counter J‑20 and J‑35 Threats</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Su‑57</span> <span>#India defence</span> <span>#aircraft procurement</span></div>
       <p>A Russian media outlet cited in Defence.in argues that India ought to procure the Su‑57 stealth fighter now to counter emerging threats from China‑Pakistan’s J‑20 and J‑35 aircraft, noting that India’s indigenous AMCA programme remains several years from operational readiness. The piece suggests that acquiring the Su‑57 would provide an immediate capability gap‑filler against advanced fifth‑generation fighters fielded by regional adversaries.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/russia-media-argues-india-should-acquire-su57-to-counter-j20.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The article stresses that the Su‑57’s advanced avionics, stealth profile and maneuverability could bolster India’s air‑defence posture while the domestic AMCA project continues development. It does not disclose specific procurement timelines, costs or official statements from Indian defence officials, focusing instead on strategic rationale.</p><p>Analysts quoted in the report warn that delaying acquisition could leave India vulnerable to air‑superiority challenges posed by the J‑20 and J‑35, emphasizing the urgency of a decision before the AMCA enters service.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft correctly attributes the claims to the Russian media outlet and accurately outlines the strategic argument provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
