       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana Launches Initiative to Boost Exports via FTAs</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana’s government is launching a new initiative to assist local industries and MSMEs in leveraging India’s free trade agreements (FTAs). Minister D. Sridhar Babu stated that the state aims to integrate local products into global supply chains by identifying district-specific goods for manufacturing and export.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/telangana-launches-initiative-to-boost-exports-via-ftas.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Speaking at an outreach program, the Minister urged the Centre to provide institutional support to help states utilize FTA benefits. Telangana plans to develop each district into an economic growth center, focusing on processing surplus agricultural produce for international markets to drive employment and strengthen the local industrial ecosystem.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately summarizes the Minister's comments and the state's strategic focus on district-specific exports and FTA utilization.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/telangana-to-help-local-industries-to-make-most-of-ftas-sridhar-babu/article71657422.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
