     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-11-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Three AAP leaders join BJP ahead of 2027 Punjab Assembly elections</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Three Aam Aadmi Party leaders, including sitting MLAs Harmeet Singh Pathanmajra and Chetan Singh Jouramajra and former legislator Kunwar Vijay Pratap Singh, joined the Bharatiya Janata Party on Monday. The defections occurred shortly after the trio was suspended by AAP for alleged anti-party activities, with the AAP seeking their disqualification from the Punjab Assembly.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/three-aap-leaders-join-bjp-ahead-of-2027-punjab-assembly-ele.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The move comes as AAP prepares for the 2027 Assembly polls, having recently released its first list of 40 candidates. The departing leaders cited concerns over drug issues, corruption, and governance, while BJP spokespersons characterized the exits as the beginning of a significant collapse for the ruling party.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the defections and the context surrounding the 2027 election preparation.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/internship-of-5-years-is-over-why-3-aap-leaders-joined-bjp-ahead-of-2027-punjab-polls-ws-l-10408393.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
