     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-11-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Two Convicted in South African Farmgate Theft</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A South African court has convicted Imanuwela David and cleaner Froliana Joseph for their roles in the 2020 theft of over $500,000 from President Cyril Ramaphosa’s Phala Phala cattle farm. David, who broke into the property and stole cash stored in a sofa, was found guilty of theft and conspiracy, while Joseph was convicted of conspiracy. The incident, which went unreported to authorities until 2022, triggered a significant political scandal and impeachment investigations against the president. While an independent panel suggested Ramaphosa faced questions regarding the burglary, he has denied any wrongdoing. Pre-sentencing for the convicted individuals is scheduled for 13 November.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/two-convicted-in-south-african-farmgate-theft.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all essential details from the source regarding the convictions and the broader political context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9vgrvpk4l6eo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
