     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-11-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>UK warns EU against protectionist industrial policies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>UK Defence Minister Wes Streeting has cautioned the European Union against excluding British companies from its &quot;Made in Europe&quot; industrial strategy. The EU initiative aims to prioritize domestic firms for public funding, sparking concerns in London that UK businesses, particularly in defense and emerging digital sectors like AI, could face systemic exclusion.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-02/uk-warns-eu-against-protectionist-industrial-policies.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These tensions precede a November 20 summit between Prime Minister Andy Burnham and EU leaders, intended to reset long-term relations. While the summit focuses on trade, youth mobility, and university fees, Britain remains wary that EU protectionism could undermine economic cooperation. Discussions regarding these digital and industrial rules are expected to continue ahead of the meeting.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the geopolitical tension regarding the EU's industrial strategy and the upcoming summit in a professional, dense format.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uk-warns-eu-against-keeping-britain-out-of-made-in-europe/article71657971.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
